Sure! Here’s a simple script that uses the 'axios' library to check the uptime of a given URL:

```javascript
const axios = require('axios');
const url = 'https://example.com';

const checkUptime = async () => {
    try {
        const response = await axios.get(url);
        console.log(`Status Code: ${response.status}`);
    } catch (error) {
        console.error(`Error: ${error.message}`);
    }
};

setInterval(checkUptime, 60000); // Check every minute
```

Make sure to add 'axios' to your dependencies by running `npm install axios`. You can configure the URL in the script.
